# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Colourspace alignment refusal (Principle 5) — this slice owns the colourspace
# reference-frame realm (gmeow:frameRealmColourspace) and its seed frames.
#
# No alignment cell is declared for the colourspace realm: no mature,
# widely-adopted RDF/OWL colourspace ontology exists to align to. ICC profiles
# are binary file formats; the CSS Color Module is a rendering spec; ONVIF
# provides only XML namespace strings. GMEOW mints its own ReferenceFrame
# individuals and points to authoritative procedural specs by reference
# (Principle 12) rather than force weak matches.
#
# REFUSED (Principle 5 — no faithful external term):
#   No external ontology provides a rigorous conceptual model of colourspace as
#   a reference system. GMEOW retains colourspace frames as canonical terms
#   without alignment.
# REFUSED (Principle 5):
#   gmeow:FrameRealm, gmeow:FrameKind, gmeow:Axis have no colourspace-specific
#   external counterparts.
